     1	//! Twofield U2 gates: APIC water transfers (P2G/G2P), grid gravity, boundary conditions.
     2	//!
     3	//! GPU-gated headless idiom — each test skips gracefully without an adapter, never
     4	//! `#[ignore]`. CPU twins of the B-spline weight kernel and a one-step P2G/G2P reference live
     5	//! at the bottom of this file and pin the GPU kernels.
     6	//!
     7	//! The free-fall reference is the solver's OWN discrete recurrence (see `transfers.wgsl`):
     8	//! per frame, P2G scatters at the old positions, the grid applies `v ← v + g·dt`, and G2P
     9	//! advects `x ← x + v_new·dt` — semi-implicit Euler, i.e. `common::freefall_reference` with
    10	//! `substeps = 1`. The weights partition unity and are linearly consistent, so the gather is
    11	//! exact for the uniform free-fall field and C stays ~0.
    12	//!
    13	//! U3 note: the frame now also runs the pressure projection, and the recurrence STILL holds
    14	//! in free flight because the projection is a no-op there to round-off: every node carrying
    15	//! mass gathers the SAME uniform velocity (momentum/mass of a uniform field is that field),
    16	//! a cell is active only when all 8 of its corner nodes carry mass, so every active cell's
    17	//! divergence — and hence the rhs, the pressure, and the projected Δv — is fixed-point noise
    18	//! (~1e-5), absorbed by the documented budgets below. The projection is gated on its own
    19	//! terms in `tests/twofield_pressure.rs`.
    20	
    21	// Axis loops (`for a in 0..3`) index several parallel arrays (positions, box bounds, grid
    22	// dims); the iterator rewrite clippy suggests obscures that symmetry.
    23	#![allow(clippy::needless_range_loop)]
